							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
							<td Width="10"></td>
							<td align="left"><span class="NewsDate" id="NewsDate">Wednesday, January 14, 2004</span>
							</td>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
							<td Width="10"></td>
							<td align="left"><span class="NewsTitle" id="NewsTitle">Changes</span>
							</td>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
							<td Width="10"></td>
							<td align="left"><span class="NewsAuthor" id="NewsAuthor">By
									Knevil
								</span>
							</td>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
							<td colspan="2" height="10"></td>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<td Width="10" bgcolor="black"></td>
							<td Width="10"></td>
							<td align="center"><div align="left">
  <p><font size="6" face="Georgia, Times New Roman, Times, serif">A</font>s the 
    holidays hit, we found ourselves struggling with our alliance. The winds of 
    change<br>
    swept in and we were forced to change our course. We chose to expand CoV's raid force<br> and kept an eye out for a similar 
    guild in need
    of our assistance.  We needed to take a<br> long hard look at where we wished to 
    go, and what we would want to see along the way.<br>  </p>
  <p> New guild rules were instituted and the applicant process was upgraded. 
    We figured to maintain<br>
    a Raid force of 35 to 40 to complement any alliance we might form. We talked 
    to and decided on <br>
    Immortal for thier talent and quality. Immortal has had a long history of 
    fighting large mobs<br>
    with little force, and a lot of talent instead. Something we always prided 
    ourselves on as well. <br>
    <br>
    This change has had us raiding more than ever. Emperor Ssra, HP, Cursed, AL 
    and VT all<br>
    night long... PoP Flaggings such as Grummus, Caprin, HoH Trials, Bertoxxolous 
    and other<br>
    smaller raids! We are really making progress as an alliance. It's been great 
    working together,<br>
    although our raid times are a bit different we seem to be making it work.<br>
  </p>
  </div>
<p align="left">We revisted Luclin and this time took on the Emperor and the Shades 
  in VT. Alot of good<br>
  has come from this and we are getting stronger and stronger. Emperor can expect 
  another<br>
  calling to see more of us join the fun. We're extremely determined there. We 
  are sure to be<br>
  set for EP's as good as most guilds shortly. Every thing ultimatly points to 
  PoT and end-game.</p>
<p align="left">&nbsp;</p>
<p><img src="http://www.circleofvalor.net/screenshots/battle.jpg" width="711" height="595"></p>
<p align="left">We suffered the departure of some newer and much older members. 
  We also have new members<br>
  joining us In December and January and would like to shout out to them!</p>
<p align="left">Welcome Archad, Alamangne, Boramen, Barsinister and Elysea! We 
  also have a list of great<br>
  applicants and are enjoying thier company on our raids as well.</p>
<p align="left">Finally! Badger Badger Badger Badger Mushroom Mushroom It's a 
  Snaaaaaaaake Snaaaaaaaaake... :) </p>
<p align="left">To recap some of the great stuff this month in VT alone...</p>
<p><img src="http://24.61.161.250/eqpics/loots.jpg"></p>
<hr>
